# Broken Access Control - IP-Based Authorization Bypass via Trusted HTTP Header

## Executive Summary

A broken access control vulnerability was identified in the application's administrative interface.

Access to the `/admin` endpoint is intended to be restricted to authenticated administrators or requests originating from the localhost interface. However, the application determines the client's IP address by trusting the value of the `X-Custom-IP-Authorization` HTTP header.

Because this header can be supplied by the client, an attacker can spoof the value `127.0.0.1` and bypass the IP-based authorization mechanism, gaining unauthorized access to the administrative panel.

This vulnerability ultimately allows an unauthenticated attacker to perform privileged administrative actions.

